<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9851" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιγρά̆φ-ω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>write against</i> or <i>in answer, write back,</i>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.129
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.86
			</span></i> W., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Luc.</u>
				21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				2.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PFlor.</u>
				278ii 30
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῆ γραφῇ</span>
			<i>vie in description</i> with painting, <i><span class="en">
				Longus
				<u>Prooem.</u>
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, with pf.
			
				Pass.
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.154
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				45.45
			</span></i>), as law-term, <i>put in as an</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιγραφή,</span>
			<i>plead against,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					11.17
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				D.
				48.31
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινί,</span> c.
				inf., <i>plead against</i> another <i>that</i>
			such is the case, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				23.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				44.39
			</span></i>:—also, <i>bring a counter-accusation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.58
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.119
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				154
			</span></i>; later in 
				Act.
			, <i>plead in answer to</i> a charge, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-γράψαι ὡς οὐκ ἔπραξεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.75
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>keep a counter-reckoning</i> of money paid or received (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιγραφεύς</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				54.3
			</span></i>; simply, <i>check</i> accounts, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				89.13
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>issue a rescript</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				888.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιγραφῆναι</span>
			<i>to be copied,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς στήλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Milet.</u>
					3.148.93
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
